flow/executor.py:282 'Substitute every ${{ … }} / ${env:VAR} in value' and lint_refs.py:61 'The ${env:VAR} literal env-indirection token'","The plan cites lint_refs.py only for the ${{ }} injection guard, not for the pre-existing ${env:VAR} handling it would duplicate — Rule-of-Three: this would be the second ${env:VAR} resolver in the codebase"],"finding":"A ${env:VAR} resolver/grammar already exists in-repo (workflow/executor.py:282 sub_env, lint_refs.py:61 _ENV_RE), but the plan proposes a new independent implementation in headers.py without citing that prior art or justifying the divergence.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9ced3b1f42110443","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Value grammar' paragraph; Scope — src/rebar/llm/headers.py (new)","norm_id":"n464b8b2be0ad7262","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two ${env:VAR} implementations drift on edge cases (nested braces, whitespace tolerance, unset-var behavior), producing inconsistent env indirection across workflow fields and headers"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to the Approach naming the existing ${env:VAR} resolver and stating whether headers.py factors out/reuses it or intentionally forks it, with the reason (e.g., ${run:...} pass-through requirement).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_impl